<!--
  Identical to values-he/. Android's resource-qualifier matching for Hebrew has never fully
  settled on "he" over the deprecated "iw" — RTL layout and Locale-based logic recognize "he"
  fine, since those go through a different, string-tag-based check, but on-device testing found
  values-he/strings.xml itself not resolving: every UI string fell back to English while
  Hebrew content (facts, video titles) from JSON assets, unaffected by this, displayed correctly.
  Shipping both costs one small duplicated file and removes the ambiguity outright.
-->
